the bellman assists the main objective  of Estonia is to develop open and  innovative European economy therefore we  plan to focus on stable growth through  promoting investments and reducing  market disruptions it should be  supported by resilient banking systems  see a tax system which takes into  account modern digital economy we talked  about the creation of the capital  markets unions it is important for  Europe to have simple access to various  funding opportunities in order to  improve the transparency of the tax  system we spoke about mandatory exchange  of information for tax advisers we  agreed on how to continue work with  non-performing loans the main problems  with impels is the fact that so far the  solutions have been sought the national  level but in this issue we need more  collective approach multi-level action  plan would help us make the financial  system stronger and prevent any problems  with non-performing loans in the future  so Europe is on the right track but we  need to accelerate our action this  action plan has four work strands on  supervisory policies on structural and  legal reforms including insolvency and  law enforcement frameworks on fostering  the secondary markets for NPS and a  support for restructuring of the banking  sector finally - formally adopted this  year's country specific recommendations  member states can now focus on reform  design and implementation the European  Commission stands ready to support this  work
 

